            ContentJson = """{"passingScore":80,"questionsPerQuiz":5,"shuffleOptions":true,"showExplanationsAfterSubmit":true,"questions":[{"id":"cq1","text":"A pool has a budget of $52,000 for the year and a driver quantity of 20,800 labor hours. What rate does the freeze derive?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"$0.40 per labor hour"},{"id":"b","text":"$2.50 per labor hour","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"$52,000 per work center"},{"id":"d","text":"It depends on the cost center's square footage"}],"explanation":"A pool's rate is Budget Amount divided by Driver Qty: 52,000 / 20,800 = $2.50 per labor hour."},{"id":"cq2","text":"You set budgets on every pool but the standard-cost rollup still shows no overhead. What did you miss?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Freezing the period on the Periods tab","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Turning on departmental rates under Admin > Costing"},{"id":"c","text":"Deleting the system template"},{"id":"d","text":"Adding square footage to the cost center"}],"explanation":"Budgets become rates only when the period is frozen. Until then there is no rate card for the rollup to use."},{"id":"cq3","text":"What does the quick start create when you apply it?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Only a costing period"},{"id":"b","text":"A PLANT cost center, a period for the fiscal year, one pool per template line, and a budget for each pool","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"A new work center for every employee"},{"id":"d","text":"A purchase order for each overhead category"}],"explanation":"The quick start builds the whole substrate in one step, sizing each budget from your headcount times 2,080 hours."},{"id":"cq4","text":"Which cost center should have Inventoriable turned off?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The plant floor"},{"id":"b","text":"The front office (SG&A)","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"The maintenance department"},{"id":"d","text":"All of them — it is only a label"}],"explanation":"Inventoriable means the cost center's overhead belongs in product cost. Selling and administrative cost is period cost and stays out of the part standard."},{"id":"cq5","text":"Under Admin > Costing, departmental mode is on and one work center's percentage is left blank. What overhead does it get?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"None — its operations carry no overhead"},{"id":"b","text":"The average of the other work centers"},{"id":"c","text":"Its own flat burden rate per hour","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"The plant cost center's total budget"}],"explanation":"A blank departmental rate falls back to the work center's flat burden rate, so nothing is left uncosted."}]}"""
